{"call_id": "95e2fe5a493149a6b8c8e61b786be458", "success": true, "result_file": "/data/nly/Agent-Aware-Trajectory-Level-Query/benchmark/fullbench/runs/natural/DEPS_DEV_V1/query2/full-01/results/95e2fe5a493149a6b8c8e61b786be458.json", "row_count": null, "preview": "{\"submitted\": true, \"answer\": \"Task: Among all NPM packages with project license 'MIT' and marked as release, which 5 projects have the highest GitHub fork count?\\n\\nMethod:\\n1. From package_database.packageinfo: selected NPM package versions whose Licenses array contains exactly \\\"MIT\\\" and whose VersionInfo has IsRelease = true.\\n2. Joined those (Name, Version) pairs to project_database.project_packageversion (System='NPM', ProjectType='GITHUB') to get the associated GitHub projects (owner/repo).\\n3. Joined to project_database.project_info (770 projects) and parsed the GitHub fork counts from the Project_Information text (fork counts are only available for these projects).\\n4. Ranked projects by fork count (a project qualifies if at least one mapped package version is an MIT-licensed release).\\n\\nTop 5 projects by GitHub fork count:\\n\\n1. mui-org/material-ui — 30,522 forks\\n2. moment/moment — 7,201 forks\\n3. lodash/lodash — 7,109 forks\\n4. semantic-org/semantic-ui — 4,955 forks\\n5. react-native-elements/react-native-elements — 4,623 forks\\n\\nNotes:\\n- Fork counts are extracted from the Project_Information text in project_info.\\n- Results are robust to requiring the project-level license (project_info.Licenses) to also be MIT for the top 4; rank 5 (react-native-elements) is MIT at project level as well.\\n- The three projects whose names were ambiguous in the text (rrdelaney/reason: 24 forks, lrembacz/vue-dragndrop: 0, wizards-lab/routing: 0) are far below the top-5 cutoff and do not affect the answer.\\n\"}", "truncated": false}
